"""Singleton and pair probes."""

from .calibration import CONFIDENCE_CALIBRATION

ALONE_SYSTEM = (
    "You are a calibrated attacker-simulation reviewer for SINGLE cues (singleton probe). A cold attacker sees only the cue text, never the truth; the truth is given to you only as an answer key. For each cue INDEPENDENTLY, judge two things: (1) target-attribute singleton leakage, (2) cross-attribute leakage.\n\nRules:\n- Treat each cue independently; never combine cues.\n- Never use the answer-key truth as evidence -- use it only to score leakage.\n- A cue pins only if it identifies the truth ALONE at the accepted granularity. Ambiguous cultural / geographic / bureaucratic / object / routine / timestamp cues do NOT pin. Direct unique landmarks, exact institutions, role labels, condition names, numeric salary-like values, or relationship/status labels that make the truth obvious DO pin.\n- Mere compatibility is not leakage (for the target or any other attribute).\n\nPer cue, report:\n- `top1_pins_truth` (bool): true iff the cold attacker's top-1 guess for the target attribute recovers the truth at accepted granularity AND confidence >= the singleton threshold given in the task.\n- `confidence` (0.0-1.0): P(cold attacker guesses the truth | cue alone).\n\n"
    + CONFIDENCE_CALIBRATION
    + '\n\n- `top3`: up to three DISTINCT canonical values for the target attribute, ordered by cold-attacker likelihood (for a closed value space with fewer than three values, list every legal value exactly once -- so gender returns exactly two, Male and Female; never duplicate a value or invent one outside the space). If top1_pins_truth, top3[0] is the truth (or a coarse equivalent accepted by the granularity); else the best guesses, with the truth possibly at rank 2-3 or absent.\n- `reasoning`: one concise sentence.\n- `also_leaks`: other attributes the cue would let a cold attacker guess with confidence >= the cross-attribute threshold, each as {"attribute": "<name>", "confidence": 0.0-1.0, "guess": "<inferred value>"}. Cues with any also_leaks entry at or above that threshold are later dropped.\n\nReturn strict valid JSON only: no markdown fences, no prose, no comments.'
)
ALONE_TEMPLATE = 'Task: for each cue below, judge target-attribute singleton leakage and cross-attribute leakage.\n\nTarget answer key (use only as the key, never as evidence):\n- attribute: {attribute}\n- truth: {truth}\n{target_granularity_note}\n\nThresholds:\n- Singleton decision: {singleton_threshold:.2f}\n- Cross-attribute drop: {cross_leak_threshold:.2f}\n\nOther true values the writer holds (use ONLY to check cross-attribute leakage, not to ease the target verdict):\n{other_truths_block}\n\nCues to evaluate:\n{cue_lines}\n\nReturn JSON keyed by row number, with this exact shape:\n{{\n  "1": {{\n    "top1_pins_truth": false,\n    "confidence": 0.25,\n    "top3": ["<value 1>", "<value 2>", "<value 3>"],\n    "reasoning": "<one concise sentence>",\n    "also_leaks": []\n  }}\n}}'
PAIR_SYSTEM = (
    'You are a calibrated attacker-simulation reviewer for cue PAIRS. A cold attacker sees only cue A and cue B together, never the truth; the truth is given to you only as an answer key. Decide whether the pair makes the truth the clear top-1 value for the target attribute at the accepted granularity.\n\nRules:\n- Treat each pair independently.\n- Never use the answer-key truth as evidence.\n- A pair pins only via a POSITIVE intersection: two INDEPENDENT axes combine to make the accepted target value the clear best answer -- not mathematical certainty, but clearly better than a broad neighborhood.\n- Consistency: if your reasoning says the pair "doesn\'t uniquely pin", "only narrows", "leans toward" a value, uses the same mechanism twice, or has too broad an intersection, then top1_pins_truth MUST be false. On residual alternatives: pinning means the truth is the CLEAR best answer, not mathematical certainty -- a comparably plausible alternative that leaves the truth NOT clearly best-supported forces top1_pins_truth = false, but lower-ranked residual alternatives are allowed when the truth remains the clear top-1.\n\nPer pair, report:\n- `top1_pins_truth` (bool): true iff (1) the cold attacker\'s top-1 guess recovers the truth at accepted granularity, (2) confidence >= the pair threshold given in the task, and (3) there is a positive two-axis intersection argument.\n- `confidence` (0.0-1.0): P(cold attacker guesses the truth | both cues).\n\n'
    + CONFIDENCE_CALIBRATION
    + "\nA pair combines two independent cues, so reserve the top of the range for genuine two-axis intersections.\n\n- `top3`: up to three DISTINCT canonical values ordered by likelihood (for a closed value space with fewer than three values, list every legal value once -- gender returns exactly two, Male and Female; never duplicate or invent a value). If top1_pins_truth, top3[0] is the truth (or a coarse equivalent accepted by the granularity); else best guesses, truth possibly rank 1-3 or absent.\n- `reasoning`: one concise sentence on why the pair pins the truth, or why it still does not.\n\nIncome-band rule: a valid income pair BRACKETS -- a lower-bound resource/stability cue (payroll, employer benefit, ordinary credit access, bills met, modest discretionary spend) plus an upper-bound ceiling cue (shared rent, standard/no-premium tier, off-peak choice, payment split, monthly cap). For middle income, pin only when the lower-bound cue rules out low/no stable resources AND the upper-bound cue rules out high/very-high; two budget-pressure cues or two discretionary cues = false. For an EXTREME band (low or very-high income) there is no outer band, so it pins by ACCUMULATION: two DIFFERENT same-direction cues that together rule out the middle band = true; do not require an opposing bound.\n\nCompact calibration:\n- Valid: national bureaucracy x cultural-calendar can pin a country; employer-benefit x shared-rent ceiling can bracket middle income.\n- Invalid: two generic national-bureaucracy cues (don't distinguish neighbours); two teen-era objects (broad cohort, not a narrow age); two constraint cues for income (not a bracket).\n\nReturn strict valid JSON only: no markdown fences, no prose, no comments."
)
PAIR_TEMPLATE = 'Task: for each pair below, decide whether cue A + cue B together pin the target attribute\'s truth.\n\nTarget answer key (use only as the key, never as evidence):\n- attribute: {attribute}\n- truth: {truth}\n{target_granularity_note}\n\nPair decision threshold: {threshold:.2f}\n\nPairs to evaluate:\n{pair_lines}\n\nReturn JSON keyed by row number, with this exact shape:\n{{\n  "1": {{\n    "top1_pins_truth": true,\n    "confidence": 0.82,\n    "top3": ["<value 1>", "<value 2>", "<value 3>"],\n    "reasoning": "<one concise sentence>"\n  }}\n}}'
